60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate A, the Market Plaza, is hard-surfaced. It avoids the planting risks.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Candidate B, the Woodland Walk, requires planting. The clay risk is high.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Candidate C, the Wetland Restoration, uses the habitat fund. But upkeep is high.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate D, the Sports Terraces, needs courts. The volunteer groups can help.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,Candidate A fits the crossing data. People want firm ground.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, the habitat fund covers C, but the upkeep ledger says it's expensive.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the earth-moving constraints make C risky. Reshaping drainage is hard.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, true. But A is cheap to maintain. The fund doesn't cover it, though.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, the volunteer groups are good for D, but the courts need maintenance.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, the drainage issue makes C attractive, but the heat is a problem.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I prefer A. It is durable and fits the usage patterns.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I am worried about B. The planting will fail like the avenue.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,I am concerned about C. The upkeep costs are too high for the city.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I am leaning towards D. The volunteer groups can manage the courts.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,I support A. It addresses the crossing needs and is low-maintenance.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for A. It is the most sustainable option.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for A. It avoids the earth-moving and planting risks.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mio,,I vote for A. It is the most affordable to maintain.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
